/// Whether a channel's address for this customer actually works.
///
/// UNKNOWN is honest rather than optimistic: nothing has been delivered and
/// nothing has failed, so sending is allowed and the first send is what finds
/// out. OK means something reached them. UNDELIVERABLE means a provider
/// reported a PERMANENT failure — a number not on WhatsApp, a mailbox that
/// does not exist — and the app stops spending money on it until the address
/// changes.
///
/// A temporary failure is deliberately not represented. A full mailbox or a
/// switched-off phone is not a wrong address, and treating it as one loses a
/// customer over a bad afternoon.
enum ReachStatus {
  UNKNOWN
  OK
  UNDELIVERABLE
}

enum ConsentStatus {
  UNKNOWN
  OPTED_IN
  OPTED_OUT
}

enum TemplateCategory {
  UTILITY
  MARKETING
  AUTHENTICATION
  SERVICE
}

enum TemplateApprovalStatus {
  DRAFT
  PENDING
  APPROVED
  REJECTED
  /// Meta pauses a template whose quality rating drops, and disables it if that
  /// continues. Both still exist on the account and neither can carry a
  /// message, so folding them into APPROVED would mean queueing sends that
  /// cannot go out.
  PAUSED
  DISABLED
}

/// WHAT A CAMPAIGN IS TRYING TO DO.
///
/// Its only real job is to suggest an attribution window, because the right
/// window is a property of the objective and nothing else: somebody nudged
/// about tomorrow's appointment either comes tomorrow or does not, while
/// somebody being won back after eight months may take a month to act. One
/// fixed fortnight for both flatters the reminder and writes off the win-back.
enum CampaignObjective {
  REMINDER
  REBOOKING
  AWARENESS
  WINBACK
  BIRTHDAY
  RENEWAL
  FESTIVAL
  REACTIVATION
  OTHER
}

/// What counts as this campaign having worked.
///
/// Separate values because they are separate things, and the code conflated
/// them: a booking is somebody deciding to come, a visit is somebody actually
/// coming, and the gap between the two is a no-show problem rather than a
/// campaign problem.
enum ConversionEvent {
  BOOKING
  VISIT
  REVENUE
}

/// A GROUP OF PEOPLE DEFINED BY WHAT THEY DID WITH A CAMPAIGN.
///
/// The point of naming these is that a campaign's recipients are not one
/// audience, they are six, and the six want completely different things next.
/// Somebody who clicked and did not book is interested and hesitating;
/// somebody the message never reached has a wrong number. Sending both the
/// same "still thinking about it?" is how a salon annoys one and wastes a
/// message on the other.
///
/// Every one of these is a LIVE rule, evaluated when it is used rather than
/// frozen when it is defined — which is what makes "stop following up once
/// they book" work without any stop logic at all: someone who books between
/// the follow-up being scheduled and it going out simply is not in the group
/// any more.
enum CampaignAudience {
  /// The provider REFUSED it — a wrong number, a dead mailbox. Something the
  /// salon can and should fix on the customer's profile.
  NOT_DELIVERED
  /// Handed over and nothing heard back.
  ///
  /// Split out from NOT_DELIVERED because collapsing the two told the salon to
  /// go and correct four perfectly good phone numbers when the real fault was
  /// a webhook that never called. "It failed" and "we have not been told" are
  /// opposite findings with opposite fixes, and one of them is not the
  /// customer's fault at all.
  AWAITING_RECEIPT
  /// Arrived, and nothing since. On WhatsApp this means no blue ticks, which
  /// is weaker evidence than it looks.
  DELIVERED_NOT_READ
  /// Read, but nothing tapped and nothing booked.
  READ_NOT_ENGAGED
  /// Tapped a button or a link, and still did not book. The warmest group
  /// that has not converted.
  ENGAGED_NOT_BOOKED
  /// Booked and has not come in yet.
  BOOKED_NOT_VISITED
  /// Came in.
  VISITED
}

enum CampaignStatus {
  DRAFT
  SCHEDULED
  RUNNING
  PAUSED
  COMPLETED
  CANCELLED
}

/// Where a message got to.
///
/// The happy path climbs: QUEUED -> SENT -> DELIVERED -> READ -> CLICKED.
/// READ means the recipient saw it — a WhatsApp read receipt or an email open;
/// they are the same fact and do not need two names.
///
/// The rest are endings rather than steps, and each says something a salon
/// would act on differently:
///
///   DELAYED     the receiving server is deferring it. Usually temporary and it
///               may still land, so it is not a failure yet.
///   BOUNCED     the address was rejected. A hard bounce means it will never
///               work and the address should stop being used.
///   COMPLAINED  they pressed "spam". Worse than a bounce: a few of these and
///               every salon on the sending domain lands in junk.
///   FAILED      we could not hand it over at all.
///   SKIPPED     never attempted — no address, no consent, no allowance.
/// WHAT A MESSAGE WAS FOR.
///
/// Category answers a billing and consent question — may we send this, and
/// what does Meta charge for it. It cannot answer the question a salon owner
/// actually asks, because UTILITY covers an appointment reminder, an invoice
/// and a "how was your visit?" all at once, and those three succeed or fail
/// for completely different reasons.
///
/// Snapshotted onto the message at send time, for the same reason category is:
/// a template can be renamed or repurposed later, and history must not move
/// with it.
enum MessagePurpose {
  /// A campaign the salon sent deliberately, to a segment.
  CAMPAIGN
  /// Appointment booked, reminded, confirmed, cancelled.
  REMINDER
  /// Invoices, receipts, payment chasers.
  BILLING
  /// "How was it?" and what follows a poor answer.
  FEEDBACK
  /// The public ask — Google, listings. Only ever after a good private answer.
  REVIEW
  /// Bringing somebody back: rebooking, win-back, expiring package or
  /// membership, birthdays, a new lead's first hello.
  FOLLOW_UP
  /// Points earned, points expiring, wallet.
  LOYALTY
  /// Sent by hand from the app, or from before purposes were recorded.
  OTHER
}

enum MessageStatus {
  QUEUED
  SENT
  DELIVERED
  READ
  CLICKED
  DELAYED
  BOUNCED
  COMPLAINED
  FAILED
  SKIPPED
}

